### Describe the bug

POST endpoint with **Content-Type:** **application/x-www-form-urlencoded** & raw **TEXT** payload (i.e., clientId & clientSecret) does not seem to get encoded and fails starting in v1.39.1, but works in previous versions including v1.38.1. I had to revert back to v1.38.1 in order for anything to work.

My sample *.bru file is below w/out credentials (clientId & clientSecret).

### .bru file to reproduce the bug

I have the following POST endpoint, AUTH.bru, for generating a jwt:

```
meta {
  name: Auth
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/authorize
  body: text
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
}

body:text {
  {
      "clientId": <SOME-CLIENT-ID>,
      "clientSecret": <SOME-SECRET>
  }
}

vars:post-response {
  TOKEN: res.body
}

```

