### Describe the feature you want to add, and how it would change your usage of Bruno

We place our Bruno collections as JSON in git. When exporting a collection again, its order of requests is shuffled completely so git diff is a mess and we cannot identify what has changed compared to the previous version.

Example export:
```json
{
  "name": "My Collection",
  "version": "1",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "folder",
      "name": "My Folder",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "http",
          "name": "a",
          "seq": 2,
          "request": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "http",
          "name": "b",
          "seq": 11,
          "request": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "http",
          "name": "c",
          "seq": 28,
          "request": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "http",
          "name": "d",
          "seq": 26,
          "request": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "http",
          "name": "e",
          "seq": 31,
          "request": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "http",
          "name": "f",
          "seq": 34,
          "request": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "http",
          "name": "g",
          "seq": 1,
          "request": {}
        },
        //...
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

As you can see the order of HTTP requests is 2, 11, 28, 26, 31, 1 ... etc. If we sort array items by seq we would maintain order and could easily identify changes in git diff.

