### Describe the bug

I want to automate a credentials grant workflow. For this, I have one request obtaining an auth token with the following Post Response script:
```js
let data = res.getBody();
bru.setEnvVar("access-token",data.access_token);
bru.setEnvVar("access-token-expiration",Date.now() + data.expires_in * 1000);
```
I use this request in the Pre Request script of another request:
```js
if (bru.getEnvVar("access-token-expiration") <= Date.now()) {
  bru.runRequest("Client credentials grant.bru")
}
```
The environment variables are successfully modified when I run the request using `bru.runRequest()`, however the second request still uses the old values.

Steps to reproduce:

1. Load the two .bru files into bruno
2. Set the environment variable `access-token-expiration` to 0
3. Set the environment variable `access-token` to something like `wrongtoken`
4. Execute `Test Environment Var Part 2` *without* executing Part 1 manually
5. Observe how the response shows that the token used was `wrongtoken` (see Authorization header)
6. Check that the environment variable `access-token` contains the value `correcttoken`

If you now run Part 2 again, it will of course use the correct value, since it is now saved in the environment variable.

Is this intended behavior? If so, how can I solve my problem in another way? Unfortunately the bru.runRequest() method does not return any response object I could use.

If possible, I would like to avoid having to manually write the authentication request code into the Pre Request script of each request that needs authentication.

Since GitHub doesn't allow me to upload .bru files as is, I will attach them as txt files and also paste their content here:

**Test Environment Var Part 1.bru**
```bruno
meta {
  name: Test Environment Var Part 1
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: https://echo.free.beeceptor.com
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "access_token": "correctttoken",
    "token_type": "Bearer",
    "expires_in": 1799
  }
}

script:post-response {
  let data = res.getBody().parsedBody;
  bru.setEnvVar("access-token",data.access_token);
  bru.setEnvVar("access-token-expiration",Date.now() + data.expires_in * 1000);
}
```

**Test Environment Var Part 2.bru**
```bruno
meta {
  name: Test Environment Var Part 2
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: https://echo.free.beeceptor.com
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access-token}}
}

script:pre-request {
  if (bru.getEnvVar("access-token-expiration") <= Date.now()) {
    bru.runRequest("Test Environment Var Part 1.bru")
  }
}
```

