### Describe the bug

Currently on v.1.37.0

## Expected behavior

I can run a .bru request in Bruno CLI, the request having `apikey` (headers) as auth mode, and said API key will get added to the request's headers.

## Observed behavior

The API key does not, in that situation, get added to the request's headers.

## Notes

The same request does in fact work in my Bruno client, and I'm able to confirm that the API key header gets added correctly there.

## Workaround

Instead of using 

```
<verb> {
  url: ...
  body: ...
  auth: apikey
}

...

auth:apikey {
  key: {{API_KEY_HEADER}}
  value: {{process.env.API_KEY_SECRET}}
  placement: header
}
```

you can set that key-value pair in the headers yourself like so

```
headers {
  {{API_KEY_HEADER}}: {{process.env.API_KEY_SECRET}}
}
```


