### Describe the bug

As I encountered in a previous issue of mine (#2528), the interpolation step for the path parameters unintentionally strips the trailing slash.

As seen here (and other instances of this code snippet):
https://github.com/usebruno/bruno/blob/8a9df14e167ff9db082495e32b02bdaf47e79257/packages/bruno-cli/src/runner/interpolate-vars.js#L102-L114

The `pathname` is split on `/`, but then the empty values are filtered out as the URL is rebuilt by prefixing values with `/` instead, causing the trailing slash to be omitted.

A solution could be to add another variable to check for a trailing slash in the original `pathname` and adding it to the final URL:
```javascript
const trailingSlash = url.pathname.endsWith('/') ? '/' : '';
request.url = url.origin + interpolatedUrlPath + trailingSlash + url.search;
```

